Forward reactions from relayed users instead of dropping them.

synccontact operators act through relay mode: each workspace has a single
shared WhatsApp login (the per-workspace bot account set as the portal relay),
and operators are separate Matrix users whose events are relayed. Upstream
bridgev2 deliberately ignores reactions (origSender != nil) because a WhatsApp
reaction can't carry per-sender attribution. In our model that attribution is
already lost for messages (relay message_formats have no sender prefix), so we
forward the reaction through the relay login, sending it as the WhatsApp
account itself. The reaction-removal (redaction) path has no relay guard, so
it already works once the reaction is stored.

